  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1021 PM CDT Thu Sep 24 2026\n\nRidging will expand west over our entire area to start the week,\nbumping our temperatures back up into the upper 80s to low 90s on\nTuesday and Wednesday. A low pressure system developing over the \nBaja California region will works its way east through the week, \neventually tracking towards the southeast. This will bring low to\nmedium 20-40% rain chances areawide back into the forecast by the\nend of the week, but this remains a low confidence forecast as \nquestions remains about how quickly this low will move and how \ndeep it will be. There is a large spread in the NBM QPF guidance \nbecause of this, so we'll have to watch how this tracks as we move\ninto next week. We would certainly benefit from the rain as all \nof Middle TN is now in some form of drought.",
